        "+++ deployed\n",
        "@@ -169,3 +169,3 @@\n",
        "     <p>I examined four practitioner reflection records alongside the student work. Notes A and B were written during the classroom inquiry. The first distinguished students’ reports of preparation from the explanations they could produce without feedback. The second documented my decision to retain original Unit 3 responses for later comparison, together with a concern that the more explicit reconstruction prompt might change what students wrote.</p>",
        "-    <p>Notes C and D were written during retrospective analysis after grades were finalized. Comparing the response pairs showed that later completeness classifications concealed different earlier relationships and contradictions. I could identify more specific questions for subsequent assessment, although I could not determine how much of the difference came from correction, the changed prompt, or other learning between attempts.</p>",
        "+    <p>Notes C and D were written during retrospective analysis after grades were finalized. Comparing the response pairs showed that later completeness classifications concealed different earlier relationships and contradictions. I could identify more specific questions for subsequent assessment, although I could not determine how much of the difference came from correction, the changed prompt, or other learning between attempts. The inquiry thus informed what I needed to investigate next without establishing the adjustment’s effect on understanding.</p>",
